begin  quoting  John H. <JohnWH@gmail.com>:
[scoring system]
>I'd say it's because that, contrary to the general current of
>opinion here in the newsgroup, the primary goal in Nethack is not
>necessarily to achieve ascension.

In conjuction with this, another proposal;

All ascensions outrank all non-ascensions. This, IMAO, is obviously a
requirement of any sane ranking system.

Score ascensions differently to non-ascensions.

That way, your argument for points for killing monsters applies - to
non-ascensions. Conversely, conducts - if scored at all - obviously apply
only to ascensions.

I would go further than my first proposal above; the topten.c limits on
scores per person/class (which should be increased anyway) apply only to
non-ascensions. The game will always track all ascensions made, albeit
perhaps reporting them in some terser format when necessary.
